ot who he succeeded. Could we use that to answer? The question: \"What United Kingdom Prime Minister was succeeded in the 1990s by the Leader of the Conservative Party?\" The answer is Margaret Thatcher, succeeded by John Major (who was Leader of Conservative Party). We need citation for Thatcher being PM before 1990. The evidence includes \"These were the first annual local elections for the new Conservative Prime Minister Margaret Thatcher.\" That shows she was PM in 1980. That indicates she was PM before 1990. So we can cite that she was PM. Also we have Major became PM in 1990. So we can answer Margaret Thatcher with citations: the 1980 local elections sentence (title \"United Kingdom local elections, 1980\", sentence 1) and the Major sentence (title \"Conservative Party (UK) leadership election, 1997\", sentence 1). That shows timeline. Provide answer \"Margaret Thatcher\"."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":466,"completion_tokens":596,"total_tokens":1062,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791982415,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}